## ⏳ What Still Needs to Be Done (Pending)

> Run these commands **in this exact order**, from the `backend` folder with `.venv` active.

### Every time you open a new terminal — activate first:
```powershell
cd "c:\Users\dilan\Downloads\complaint-classifier (2)\Sana_complaint-classifier\backend"
.venv\Scripts\activate
```
✅ You'll see `(.venv)` at the start of the line when it's active.

---

### Step 1 — Generate the dataset (run ONCE)
```powershell
python -m ml.generate_data
```
**What it does:** Creates `backend/data/complaints.csv` with 640 synthetic civic complaints across 8 categories.

---

### Step 2 — Train the ML classifier (run ONCE)
```powershell
python -m ml.train_classifier
```
**What it does:** Trains a Logistic Regression model on sentence embeddings. Saves `backend/models/classifier.joblib`. Takes ~2–5 minutes (downloads the embedding model on first run).

---

### Step 3 — Build the FAISS search index (run ONCE)
```powershell
python -m ml.build_index
```
**What it does:** Converts all 640 complaints into 384-dim vectors and stores them in `backend/models/complaints.faiss`.

---

### Step 4 — Seed demo map data (run ONCE, optional but recommended)
```powershell
python seed_demo.py
```
**What it does:** Adds 12 sample map reports around Bengaluru so the map has pins to look at. Also creates two demo accounts:
- Email: `demo.reporter@example.com` | Password: `demo-pass-123`
- Email: `demo.neighbour@example.com` | Password: `demo-pass-123`

---

### Step 5 — Start the server 🚀
```powershell
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```
**What it does:** Starts the FastAPI web server. Keep this terminal open while using the app.

---

### Step 6 — Open in browser 🌐
```
http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

